  "title": "# Build: readme-rule-every-build (Opus, low thinking; tiny rules change) ## What Brett said (verbat…",
  "asked": "# Build: readme-rule-every-build (Opus, low thinking; tiny rules change) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"We gotta structure the documentation engine later anyway, so leave that out. Just get basic documentation. In Markdown.\" Asked whether every future build should include a basic Markdown readme: \"Yeah.\" Book to a free named agent. ## Do - Add a standing rule to `_claude/rules/RULES.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and every build-brief template/boilerplate the orchestrator and build_start use: **every build ships a basic Markdown readme for what it adds or changes, in the same PR**: `docs/README.md` inside the plugin/app/module folder (or a section added to an existing one). It covers what it does, how to use it (screens, settings, right-click actions, voice commands), commands (API/MCP/CLI) and troubleshooting. Plain Markdown, no docs engine. - Add a light CI check: a PR that adds a new plugin/app/module folder without a `docs/README.md` fails. Existing folders are grandfathered. - No documentation-engine work. That's planned separately. - PR, auto-land when green. Short report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
